<title>GREECE: Greece sells more than 250 bln drs of T-notes.</title>
<headline>Greece sells more than 250 bln drs of T-notes.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Greek finance ministry said in a statement that investors bought more than 250 billion drachmas worth of two-year zero coupon T-notes that hit the market today.</p>
<p>The pre-tax yield to maturity of two-year zeros was 10.30 percent.</p>
<p>The finance ministry said it filled its coffers with more than 530 billion drachmas which represented 27 percent of the annual sale target for this type of security in January. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
